From 258e665bf494547283f57d22e9dc44786a31dfef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas <yusenrong46@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:43:16 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Redesign Luna chat around the conversation, one offer and
 one check-in

Chat shell: compact header; the log keeps the newest message in view only while
the person is at the bottom (a 'New messages' prompt otherwise); the composer
stays focused and read-only during a reply instead of disabled, grows with the
draft, and follows the visual viewport so a mobile keyboard cannot hide it.

Activity: one offer card (Start activity / Something else / Just talk or Not now);
started activities move to a compact bar above the composer (timer ring, Pause or
Resume, Finish early, Stop, Steps) via a portal, so the conversation is no longer
buried; the single check-in keeps every API field but puts optional detail behind
'Add more detail'; the receipt shows until Luna's follow-up arrives. Search has one
entry point in AI chats (the separate library stays on Home). Expiry uses an
explicit effect dependency instead of running after every timer repaint.

Journal: the source strip shows the entry date and how long ago it was written and
says how you feel now may differ.

Bug fix: with an entry chooser open over an unrelated chat, the composer stayed
enabled and sent into that chat without the entry. It now waits for a choice.

Accessibility: typing indicator is a status, menus are named, sage tag text meets
AA, and every tour state is checked with axe. Selector updates in integration
tests follow the moved controls; behavioural assertions are unchanged.

Verified: 114 unit, 46 e2e, 18 integration plus 4 tour checks with axe on local
PostgreSQL (Luna, Brave and auth are stand-ins).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
